You can use a hand behind the back or a hooking foot as an easier progression.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MpfpSkwcqsg', null, null, 13, 1, 1, 1);

Do a Rocket Mount the same as you always would until the end where you would usually push the line downwards to mount it.

Instead of pushing the line downwards you want to push it away from you like a bench press. You will immediately start rotating if your timing is correct.

Once you''re getting the rotation start looking at the line so you can spot putting your feet on the line. You will likely miss the first few times and end up in sofa.

With good technique this trick can be done with no-bounce like a Rocket Mount.

At first you''ll probably need a lot of bounce with bad technique but as it gets better you want to dial it back otherwise you''ll get launched off when you land.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r5rwYkvnbco', null, null, 9, 5, 1, 1);

Despite this trick being in a relatively high tier its only real prerequisite is bouncing in exposure.

Many people get this as their first trick despite the difficulty since it has no real technical requirements.

Getting it consistent however is a long journey.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DgVLWsChXFM', null, null, 5, 5, 1, 1);

